1
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:07,980
When I participated in Walpurgis,

2
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:11,980
I defeated Clayman, was formally 
recognized as a Demon Lord,

3
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:15,900
and became part of Octagram, 
the Eight-Star Demon Lords.

4
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:28,590
My business here is done. I'm leaving.

5
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:34,120
Leon and Valentine left as soon 
as the conference ended.

6
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:38,720
Afterward, Guy put on a dinner party 
for those who remained...

7
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:41,720
This is stewed black-furred tiger.

8
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:45,240
This is good!

9
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:48,610
The meat falls apart on my tongue, 
and the sauce coats it...

10
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:49,950
Raphael-sensei!

11
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:52,600
Understood. Analyzing the recipe.

12
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:56,280
Looks like we don't need 
to worry about manners here.

13
00:00:57,270 --> 00:00:59,350
Hey, Milim! That's alcohol!

14
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:01,770
What's the problem?

15
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:04,410
It's my reward for pretending 
to be manipulated!

16
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:08,410
Couldn't you have stopped 
pretending sooner, though?

17
00:01:08,410 --> 00:01:11,540
Clayman never did open up 
about who was pulling the strings.

18
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:15,680
Indeed! But it was a welcome chance 
to battle against Rimuru!

19
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:16,300
Hey!

20
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,040
You can't have this yet!

21
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:20,280
Meanie!

22
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:23,460
I'm the oldest Demon Lord, 
despite how I look!

23
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:24,110
It really is good brandy.

24
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:27,030
It doesn't matter if it's alcohol 
or anything else! It's nothing to me!

25
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:27,020
Is it made with grapes from Eurazania?

26
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:28,660
I'm impressed you could tell.

27
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:32,520
We can finally make it consistently now, 
thanks to the fruit we import from them.

28
00:01:32,850 --> 00:01:35,510
Well, then, I'll have one more!

29
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:38,410
You need to learn restraint!

30
00:01:38,410 --> 00:01:40,410
Ugh, this is strong...

31
00:01:40,770 --> 00:01:43,680
You're pathetic! Just watch this!

32
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:49,920
Valentine would definitely 
like this. What a waste.

33
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:49,240
Gimme another!

34
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,880
Valentine, huh?

35
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:54,560
There was a lot I wanted to ask her...

36
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,800
Oh, well.

37
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:56,570
Notice.

38
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:56,340
Notice

39
00:01:56,570 --> 00:01:58,480
Analysis complete.

40
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,270
It is now possible to recreate 
the full dinner course.

41
00:02:01,270 --> 00:02:04,800
I've got some of 
the best recipes in the world,

42
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:07,090
and I made it through Walpurgis.

43
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:06,580
Lady Ramiris...

44
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:08,690
We must tell her about that...

45
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:13,040
And now, I've come back home to Tempest.

46
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:32,460
That Time I Got 
Reincarnated as a Slime

47
00:03:44,450 --> 00:03:49,950
Episode 49: Demons and Strategies

48
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,500
We're open today!

49
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:52,990
Wait up!

50
00:03:59,630 --> 00:04:00,670
Huh?

51
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:05,640
What's this all about?

52
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:09,350
When did you guys practice for this?

53
00:04:09,350 --> 00:04:11,960
Great Rimuru!

54
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:15,440
Welcome home, Great Rimuru!

55
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:20,460
My most sincere congratulations 
on your succession to Octagram.

56
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:22,210
Oh... Thanks.

57
00:04:22,210 --> 00:04:25,690
Above all, I am so glad 
that you have returned safely.

58
00:04:25,910 --> 00:04:29,030
Wait, Diablo, what are you doing here?

59
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:32,250
Now, now. You must be exhausted.

60
00:04:32,250 --> 00:04:35,540
For now, just take your 
time recovering your energy.

61
00:04:40,930 --> 00:04:41,970
Come in.

62
00:04:41,970 --> 00:04:43,220
Pardon me.

63
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:52,300
Oh, is this matcha pudding?

64
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:53,340
Yes.

65
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:55,440
I'm not as good as Princess Shuna yet,

66
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:57,440
but I have gotten better at cooking.

67
00:04:57,440 --> 00:05:00,780
Oh? I assume you brought some for me, too?

68
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:03,080
Of course, Lord Veldora.

69
00:05:03,890 --> 00:05:05,340
Lord Veldora.

70
00:05:05,730 --> 00:05:09,040
This is your promised portion, the first.

71
00:05:11,070 --> 00:05:14,800
Diablo, you seem to be a man 
with a strong sense of duty.

72
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:17,790
Diablo, aren't you going to eat some?

73
00:05:17,790 --> 00:05:21,130
This is my payment 
to him in return for information.

74
00:05:21,130 --> 00:05:23,160
You need not worry about me.

75
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:25,000
Information?

76
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:29,000
Whistle, whistle...

77
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,760
I wondered how Diablo knew 
about what was decided at Walpurgis.

78
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:35,440
How many desserts did you sell it for?

79
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:38,500
One? Two? Three?

80
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:39,360
Yep, three.

81
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:43,980
But, Veldora, you don't 
even need to eat, do you?

82
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:46,690
D-Don't be ridiculous, Rimuru!

83
00:05:46,690 --> 00:05:49,940
It's not a matter 
of whether I need to eat or not!

84
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:52,280
I eat because I want to eat!

85
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:55,970
Besides, you don't need 
to eat, either, do you?!

86
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:03,800
You did escort Great 
Rimuru properly, I presume?

87
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,300
Of course I did.

88
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:09,200
I proved that he doesn't 
need you as long as he has me.

89
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:10,680
But that aside,

90
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:14,340
what became of the task 
Great Rimuru assigned to you?

91
00:06:16,370 --> 00:06:18,350
Completed to perfection.

92
00:06:18,350 --> 00:06:21,850
I don't get how you timed your 
return so perfectly, though.

93
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:24,160
I was taking care of other matters,

94
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:27,360
but Lord Veldora contacted me 
and advised me to return.

95
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:31,540
I-I just remembered 
something I need to do...

96
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:35,680
Now, just sit tight, Veldora-kun.

97
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:38,100
W-Wait... You'll understand 
when I explain...

98
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:41,040
Like hell I will! 
Don't butt into other people's work!

99
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:42,670
No pudding for you!

100
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:46,170
Haruna-san, don't give 
Veldora any snacks for a while.

101
00:06:46,170 --> 00:06:49,920
What?! That's cruel! 
That's too cruel, Rimuru!

102
00:06:50,170 --> 00:06:51,930
I can't be bothered anymore.

103
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:55,930
Anyway, should you be wasting time here?

104
00:06:55,930 --> 00:06:58,050
Is everything okay with Falmuth?

105
00:06:58,050 --> 00:06:59,120
Hmph!

106
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:02,100
A tea server is better off serving tea.

107
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:04,980
Allow me to take care of this matter.

108
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:07,640
There will be no need for that.

109
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:12,410
With my informant on the job, 
all is proceeding as planned.

110
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:14,400
It is?

111
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,420
Yes.

112
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:19,290
For starters, I restored all of them 
to their original forms.

113
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:22,530
It was inconvenient 
to leave them as lumps of flesh.

114
00:07:22,530 --> 00:07:23,930
Lumps of flesh?

115
00:07:23,930 --> 00:07:26,540
Oh, I get it.

116
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,400
My goodness.

117
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:31,210
Miss Shion is such a troublemaker.

118
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,500
What a hassle.

119
00:07:36,850 --> 00:07:40,440
Healing magic is not even effective on you.

120
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:45,850
What sort of skill bends all 
the rules to this extent?

121
00:07:47,690 --> 00:07:51,360
I'll need to take some drastic 
measures. Try to endure it.

122
00:07:56,720 --> 00:08:01,290
You think the three in that carriage 
are gonna make it to Falmuth in one piece?

123
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:04,000
I'm not sure you could say 
they're in one piece now.

124
00:08:06,050 --> 00:08:07,260
Thank you!

125
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:10,050
Thank you, Lord Diablo!

126
00:08:10,050 --> 00:08:11,760
Shut up, trash.

127
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:14,130
Now, who's next?

128
00:08:15,610 --> 00:08:18,140
Restore the king before me...

129
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:20,350
Return him to his original form...

130
00:08:20,350 --> 00:08:24,590
Oh, yes. I nearly forgot you 
were one of the prisoners.

131
00:08:24,590 --> 00:08:27,850
Your name was Ramen... 
I mean, Razen, correct?

132
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,760
You do understand, of course,

133
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:35,480
that asking a favor of me comes 
at a very high price?

134
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,870
That's right... This man...

135
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:42,240
He's Noir, one of 
the seven Primordial Demons.

136
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:44,920
But what's truly terrifying is...

137
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:49,050
that there's someone this demon serves!

138
00:08:49,770 --> 00:08:52,040
Shion, don't overdo it.

139
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:57,760
A Demon Lord possessing a hidden power that, 
while fleeting, surpasses imagination.

140
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:59,810
I knew in that moment

141
00:08:59,810 --> 00:09:04,120
that the Kingdom of Falmuth 
had awakened a sleeping lion.

142
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:10,900
Take me... no.

143
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:15,200
Please accept me as your 
lowest-ranked servant.

144
00:09:15,450 --> 00:09:19,050
I will devote every 
aspect of my life to you.

145
00:09:19,050 --> 00:09:22,770
So please, show King Edmaris mercy!

146
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:25,840
Very well, then.

147
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:30,760
However, I will not tolerate further 
disrespect toward Great Rimuru.

148
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:35,140
If I detect any malice, 
the king will not be the only one to die.

149
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:39,510
You can expect the breath of life to vanish 
from the land of Falmuth itself.

150
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:43,760
Of course. My loyalty is yours alone.

151
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,730
M-Me, too!

152
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:49,320
I am the Archbishop 
of the Western Holy Church!

153
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:51,360
I can surely be of use to you!

154
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:56,690
A royal mage who served 
the royal family for so long

155
00:09:56,690 --> 00:10:00,370
has at last turned his back 
on the Kingdom of Falmuth.

156
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:06,870
You sullied Great Rimuru's 
beautiful hands with human blood!

157
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:11,330
This is the fate you and I must bear.

158
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:16,840
I'm sure Razen's decision was the right one.

159
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:22,090
As the last king of Falmuth...

160
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:31,080
I swear to cooperate in any 
way you desire, Lord Diablo.

161
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:33,830
Worry not.

162
00:10:33,830 --> 00:10:37,610
So long as you obey me, 
I will treat you well.

163
00:10:41,630 --> 00:10:45,360
With my unique skill Tempter,

164
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:45,370
TEMPTER

165
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:48,370
preventing betrayal is a simple matter.

166
00:10:50,090 --> 00:10:52,460
Hey, Diablo!

167
00:10:52,460 --> 00:10:54,670
The prisoners are alive, right?

168
00:10:54,670 --> 00:10:56,960
Not to worry, Sir Youm.

169
00:10:57,270 --> 00:10:59,480
We will soon reach the capital of Falmuth.

170
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:01,130
Taking over a country is trivial.

171
00:11:01,130 --> 00:11:03,430
Let us get it over with quickly.

172
00:11:03,430 --> 00:11:04,680
S-Sure.

173
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,600
No matter what magic we use,

174
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,980
he won't return to his original form...

175
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:21,380
Shogo, what is the meaning of this?

176
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:25,370
Where are the other two? 
What happened to the royal army?

177
00:11:25,370 --> 00:11:28,200
Calm down. I'm Razen.

178
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:32,620
To protect the king, I cooperated 
with the champion to escape.

179
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:37,000
What? You're saying that you aren't Shogo?

180
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
And you say the Falmuth army was defeated?

181
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,260
Don't tell me you failed 
to subjugate the monsters,

182
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:45,040
and you had the nerve 
to run back home in disgrace?!

183
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:45,680
What?!

184
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:46,930
Surely not!

185
00:11:46,930 --> 00:11:47,930
What is the meaning of this?!

186
00:11:47,930 --> 00:11:50,360
Calm down, gentlemen.

187
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:53,750
Let us hear what Sir Razen has to say first.

188
00:11:57,640 --> 00:12:00,720
All of them went missing? Is this true?

189
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:01,830
It is.

190
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:04,910
Our army's battle with the monsters

191
00:12:04,910 --> 00:12:07,910
awakened a dragon 
that was sleeping in this land.

192
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:12,910
But the Western Holy Church said 
the dragon was destroyed!

193
00:12:12,910 --> 00:12:15,350
It was indeed destroyed,

194
00:12:15,350 --> 00:12:17,970
but a dragon factor does not die.

195
00:12:17,970 --> 00:12:20,920
The dragon will simply be 
reborn elsewhere in the world.

196
00:12:21,570 --> 00:12:24,600
We simply didn't expect it 
to return so soon,

197
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:28,180
or in a place so close to us.

198
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:30,210
With the return of Veldora,

199
00:12:30,210 --> 00:12:33,440
all the knights and monsters 
in that area disappeared.

200
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:35,810
We were the only ones left.

201
00:12:35,810 --> 00:12:36,710
Impossible!

202
00:12:36,710 --> 00:12:37,720
It can't be...

203
00:12:40,860 --> 00:12:42,660
Sorry I'm late.

204
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:49,360
I managed to convince you-know-who.

205
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:53,770
Who do you think you are?!

206
00:12:53,770 --> 00:12:55,670
How dare a bunch 
of commoners barge in here?!

207
00:12:55,670 --> 00:12:57,830
Please hold, Lord Carlos.

208
00:12:57,830 --> 00:13:00,840
They are the ones who saved us.

209
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:03,880
They saved you, you say?

210
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:06,080
What do you mean by that?

211
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:09,090
Allow me to answer that.

212
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:10,930
Archbishop Reyhiem!

213
00:13:14,050 --> 00:13:16,730
When the two armies 
clashed on the battlefield,

214
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:19,440
the battle that broke out was intense.

215
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:22,480
We had the advantage in numbers,

216
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:25,000
but it was no match 
for the monsters' knowledge of the land,

217
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,200
and many of our men were lost.

218
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:32,730
The chaos that ensued must have been 
the key to its resurrection.

219
00:13:32,730 --> 00:13:35,250
With the sudden appearance of Veldora,

220
00:13:35,250 --> 00:13:36,960
everyone there, both friend and foe,

221
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:41,960
was resolved to die 
in the presence of the Storm Dragon.

222
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,550
But just then,

223
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:46,000
someone stood between us and the dragon!

224
00:13:47,410 --> 00:13:51,960
That someone was 
the monsters' leader, Great Rimuru.

225
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:55,520
Both Archbishop Reyhiem 
and I were prepared to die.

226
00:13:55,520 --> 00:14:00,520
But Great Rimuru convinced 
Veldora to let us live.

227
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:04,110
He was able to speak with him?!

228
00:14:04,110 --> 00:14:07,810
But just being in contact 
with the Evil Dragon's dense magicules

229
00:14:07,810 --> 00:14:10,390
means instant death for most living things!

230
00:14:10,390 --> 00:14:12,240
So how...

231
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,970
Surely all of you are aware

232
00:14:14,970 --> 00:14:20,000
that the monsters' leader is also 
the ruler of the Great Forest of Jura.

233
00:14:20,310 --> 00:14:23,370
He wasn't just calling 
himself that on his own?

234
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:27,140
Most certainly not!

235
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:29,410
I saw the city of monsters myself,

236
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:32,760
and it was truly worthy of being called 
the capital of a nation.

237
00:14:33,030 --> 00:14:38,600
Even the Dryads, the guardians 
of the Great Forest of Jura, serve him!

238
00:14:38,950 --> 00:14:44,110
It was through the Dryads that 
Great Rimuru negotiated with Veldora.

239
00:14:44,370 --> 00:14:45,920
Dryads?

240
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:49,440
They are powerful monsters that 
protect the land where Veldora sleeps.

241
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:51,860
He even commands beings as powerful as them?

242
00:14:52,210 --> 00:14:55,360
If this Rimuru can negotiate 
with the Evil Dragon,

243
00:14:55,360 --> 00:15:00,130
we definitely do not want to 
make an enemy of him.

244
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:05,120
Whoa, guys. You don't 
have to worry about that.

245
00:15:05,430 --> 00:15:10,790
I worked with Rimuru 
when I defeated the Orc Lord.

246
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:13,320
He's friendlier than you'd think,

247
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,840
and he wants to live in harmony with humans.

248
00:15:16,110 --> 00:15:21,500
Oh, then you can serve as the mediator 
who conveys our demands to him.

249
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:24,340
I will let you know what they are later.

250
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:25,860
Wait in another room for now.

251
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:28,480
Hang on just a minute.

252
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:32,520
He's friendly under normal 
circumstances, but not now.

253
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:35,360
And I'm pretty sure you know why.

254
00:15:35,570 --> 00:15:36,870
Excuse me?!

255
00:15:36,870 --> 00:15:41,140
You're the ones who declared war 
on Rimuru's nation, aren't you?

256
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:42,620
That was a bad idea.

257
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:46,370
Some of Rimuru's friends 
died because of that.

258
00:15:46,370 --> 00:15:48,680
He's pissed as hell right now.

259
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:51,640
Watch your tongue, commoner!

260
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:54,640
If you have clout with this Rimuru, 
that suits our purposes!

261
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:57,080
It's your duty as champion 
to mediate for us!

262
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:58,270
So do something!

263
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:00,890
Lord Carlos, stand down!

264
00:16:00,890 --> 00:16:04,400
Okay, first of all, listen to me.

265
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:07,600
You sent Otherworlders 
to wreak havoc in his nation

266
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:10,520
without sending messengers 
or declaring war first, right?

267
00:16:10,950 --> 00:16:13,520
I went out there to try to make peace,

268
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:16,320
but when I heard about that, I was shocked.

269
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:20,630
Still, I was born here 
in the Kingdom of Falmuth.

270
00:16:20,630 --> 00:16:23,280
I didn't want to see my 
homeland get destroyed,

271
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:26,330
so I pleaded with him 
to make some sort of deal.

272
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:30,670
A commoner has no right 
to speak of our kingdom's cause!

273
00:16:30,670 --> 00:16:32,400
Listen here! I refuse to—

274
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:33,800
I told you to stand down!

275
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:36,040
You absolute moron!

276
00:16:37,550 --> 00:16:40,430
You have no clue what went 
down, so just butt out!

277
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:49,610
Listen to me, everyone. 
What Sir Youm says is true.

278
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,010
We were defeated.

279
00:16:52,010 --> 00:16:54,610
The only survivors were 
Archbishop Reyhiem, myself,

280
00:16:54,610 --> 00:16:57,320
and King Edmaris, 
who was transformed into this

281
00:16:57,320 --> 00:17:01,120
after coming in contact 
with the Storm Dragon's magicules.

282
00:17:01,290 --> 00:17:02,960
We were imprisoned,

283
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:06,960
and it was Sir Youm who 
recommended we be set free.

284
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:11,560
The great Kingdom of Falmuth, 
overpowered by a nation of monsters?

285
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:14,100
Yet we have no choice.

286
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:17,860
Do you intend to make 
an enemy of the Storm Dragon?

287
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:19,090
Well, I...

288
00:17:19,430 --> 00:17:24,000
Let us accept his offer. Right, gentlemen?

289
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:30,740
A wise decision.

290
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:35,780
Now, as promised, I will 
set this nation's king free.

291
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:36,630
Who are you?!

292
00:17:36,630 --> 00:17:38,110
When did you—

293
00:17:38,850 --> 00:17:42,080
I do apologize, but you were wide open.

294
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,200
My name is Diablo.

295
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:50,630
I am my king Great Rimuru's loyal butler.

296
00:17:53,370 --> 00:17:54,380
Your Majesty!

297
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:55,880
Wh-What is that medicine?

298
00:17:56,990 --> 00:18:00,320
A full potion, a local 
specialty of our nation.

299
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:02,800
The best healing medicine there is.

300
00:18:04,270 --> 00:18:06,500
How are you feeling?

301
00:18:08,810 --> 00:18:11,560
You've saved me. Thank you.

302
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:13,960
Now, King of Falmuth,

303
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:18,070
I have a message for you 
from my king, Great Rimuru.

304
00:18:18,830 --> 00:18:22,570
Speak, messenger 
from the nation of monsters.

305
00:18:23,070 --> 00:18:25,540
Very well. I shall.

306
00:18:25,830 --> 00:18:27,560
"One week from now,

307
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:31,550
representatives from both our nations 
will meet in this land to discuss peace.

308
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:34,540
I will give you options."

309
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:36,300
Options?

310
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:40,950
"Option one: your king abdicates the throne 
and pays reparations to us.

311
00:18:40,950 --> 00:18:45,300
Option two: you surrender to our nation 
and become a vassal state.

312
00:18:45,630 --> 00:18:48,640
Option three: the war continues."

313
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:51,060
He's mad...

314
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:52,980
"These are your options.

315
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:57,120
Please have your answer 
ready within one week."

316
00:18:58,070 --> 00:19:00,780
Wait a moment! That's not enough time!

317
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:02,150
Quiet.

318
00:19:02,150 --> 00:19:04,530
I have a very short temper.

319
00:19:04,530 --> 00:19:07,630
But we must summon nobles 
from all regions...

320
00:19:08,590 --> 00:19:10,540
I told you to be quiet.

321
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:15,830
What you want means nothing to Great Rimuru.

322
00:19:15,830 --> 00:19:17,040
Understand?

323
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:20,560
So don't even think 
about pulling any petty tricks.

324
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:23,880
You will not be permitted 
to delay your answer.

325
00:19:24,670 --> 00:19:26,950
If you give no answer in one week,

326
00:19:26,950 --> 00:19:29,640
we will assume you intend 
to continue the war.

327
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:31,020
Is that clear?

328
00:19:31,290 --> 00:19:35,520
Now then, think very carefully 
about your answer.

329
00:19:40,450 --> 00:19:43,580
And that is what I did 
to throw them off-balance.

330
00:19:43,580 --> 00:19:45,370
You showed them that?

331
00:19:45,370 --> 00:19:46,080
Yes.

332
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:49,830
I determined that it was the best way 
to strike fear into them.

333
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:53,080
He wasn't complimenting you, Shion.

334
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:56,090
Now, as for the peace terms...

335
00:19:56,090 --> 00:20:00,130
I demanded ten thousand stellar 
gold coins as reparations.

336
00:20:01,130 --> 00:20:02,850
It's no use...

337
00:20:01,130 --> 00:20:02,850
Ten thousand stellar gold coins?!

338
00:20:02,850 --> 00:20:04,880
I have no hopes or dreams left...

339
00:20:02,850 --> 00:20:04,880
That's, uh...

340
00:20:04,930 --> 00:20:09,140
100 million × 10 rows × 100 layers

341
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:07,030
Expressed in terms of Japanese yen,

342
00:20:07,030 --> 00:20:09,150
the approximate value is one trillion.

343
00:20:09,150 --> 00:20:10,120
Huh?!

344
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:12,560
Don't you think that was a bit unreasonable?

345
00:20:12,810 --> 00:20:14,540
Not a problem.

346
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:16,790
I gave them three options,

347
00:20:16,790 --> 00:20:18,900
but there is only one correct answer.

348
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:31,910
Surrender to Tempest 
and become a vassal state

349
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:31,910
King abdicates and
pays reparations

350
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:31,910
War continues

351
00:20:19,230 --> 00:20:23,720
The continuation of the war is impossible, 
with their army destroyed.

352
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:28,320
And it's obvious that their nobles 
will oppose becoming a vassal state.

353
00:20:28,320 --> 00:20:31,910
Which means they'll choose 
option one—reparations—

354
00:20:31,910 --> 00:20:35,410
and they will make every 
effort to negotiate.

355
00:20:35,630 --> 00:20:39,920
Like, to lower the amount or let them 
pay in installments for ten years?

356
00:20:40,150 --> 00:20:42,080
We will not agree to lower the amount.

357
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:45,290
The Kingdom of Falmuth will have no choice 
but to accept our terms.

358
00:20:45,290 --> 00:20:51,290
They will most likely go about it by forcing 
all responsibility upon a third party.

359
00:20:51,290 --> 00:20:53,310
And what happens then?

360
00:20:53,310 --> 00:20:54,960
Exactly what I've planned.

361
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:58,940
We should be able to collect ten thousand 
stellar gold coins, at least.

362
00:20:58,940 --> 00:21:00,410
How do you know?

363
00:21:00,410 --> 00:21:01,900
Simple.

364
00:21:02,270 --> 00:21:05,830
Stellar gold coins are so valuable, 
they're difficult to use.

365
00:21:05,830 --> 00:21:08,400
It's unlikely anyone would 
accept them as payment.

366
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,680
I get it.

367
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:12,740
We'd have no way to use them, 
so we'd have to save them up.

368
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:15,490
And what else are you plotting?

369
00:21:17,230 --> 00:21:23,080
Choosing the first option means they 
pay reparations and their king abdicates.

370
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:26,270
After abdicating, Edmaris will lose 
the basis of his influence,

371
00:21:26,510 --> 00:21:30,810
and he will be coerced 
into assuming responsibility.

372
00:21:30,810 --> 00:21:36,020
So he's the third party that 
the nobles will force the responsibility on.

373
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:38,140
Now that their royal knights are gone,

374
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:43,670
opposing the nobles would 
mean death for King Edmaris.

375
00:21:43,670 --> 00:21:45,950
He'll have no choice but to do as they say.

376
00:21:46,230 --> 00:21:50,600
But that would only be on the surface. 
Behind the scenes...

377
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:54,340
With no military, the king's faction 
lose to the nobles' faction.

378
00:21:54,340 --> 00:21:55,960
And to avoid that...

379
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:57,030
Answer.

380
00:21:57,030 --> 00:21:59,720
The optimal method is 
to absorb Youm's faction

381
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:02,400
and maintain a cooperative partnership.

382
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,710
By doing so...

383
00:22:03,710 --> 00:22:05,910
King Edmaris would have to 
make an ally of Youm...

384
00:22:05,910 --> 00:22:09,340
or in other words, allies of us all.

385
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:12,190
Precisely. Most impressive.

386
00:22:12,190 --> 00:22:15,680
So we'd just need to lend 
Youm some of our forces, right?

387
00:22:15,910 --> 00:22:16,800
Yes.

388
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:20,200
I expect Razen to contact me soon.

389
00:22:20,410 --> 00:22:22,440
Would that be enough for us to win?

390
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:25,160
What kind of face am I even supposed

391
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:25,160
Their next king won't form an alliance

392
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:26,460
to make right now?

393
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:27,440
with the surrounding nations?

394
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:31,450
Sir Fuze and King Gazel, their neighbors, 
are using their influence

395
00:22:31,450 --> 00:22:33,440
to put pressure on their other neighbors.

396
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:37,240
So the chances of that are very low,

397
00:22:38,210 --> 00:22:42,180
but if it does happen, 
I will handle it personally.

398
00:22:42,180 --> 00:22:43,720
You need not worry.

399
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,670
Okay, I'll leave it to you.

400
00:22:45,670 --> 00:22:47,720
Contact me if anything comes up.

401
00:22:47,720 --> 00:22:51,720
Of course. Please leave 
everything to me, my king.

402
00:24:25,300 --> 00:24:28,320
Next time, "The Saint's Intentions."

403
00:24:25,980 --> 00:24:29,940
The Saint's Intentions

